# HL-LN (the Lever N hang shapes and the skewed eight, on the TRAFFIC profile the image bakes in, a FRESH boot): the decoder finishes, all decoders finish, a cancel mid-prefill, an arrival during a prefill, the seed stops,
# the eight steady, the drain and the skew. THREE jobs, each after its own reset: the rule is three CONSECUTIVE completions (G-NP3: two partial prefills in the runner's persistent batch is the design's first-listed
# risk). READ: every user at budget, no refusal, no hang (no host block in execute_trace, no watchdog dump), no garbage or empty stream, no program compiled after the warm; one stall stops the candidate.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-2 window pack (tp4-w2-levern-jobs: Lever N robustness, then the cutover; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,levern_decoder_finishes,levern_all_decoders_finish,levern_cancel_mid_prefill,levern_arrival_during_prefill,levern_seed_stops,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_skew
C2_BOX_MINUTES=55
